WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.230
- It's a good reminder that things...

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.803
Things were good, and will be again.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:08.543
They are good.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:15.303
(inspiring music)

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.640
- I'm Sara Piergiuseppe, and
today I'm gonna be looking at

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.140
my wedding pictures with my ex-husband.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.030
- This should be interesting.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.130
- We met through friends.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.330
Well, technically, we met in
a bar, but we knew people,

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.820
so it feels a little less sleazy.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.370
- She had a red top on.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:42.060
I was smitten from go,
and she was playing it

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:42.980
to cool for school.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.970
- It was not a match, at first.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.510
I really wasn't interested,
but he grew on me,

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.920
and he asked me out,
probably like a month later.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.200
- Our first date was on August the 9th.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.640
- The rest is history, and now we're here.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.310
- Within, I'd say, about a year of dating,

00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.410
we moved in together.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:03.150
- And then we got engaged, it
was a year and a half later.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.940
- New Year's Eve, at a
Black Crowes concert,

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.017
after one too many drinks, I said to her,

00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:12.887
"I have no ring, I have no money--"

00:01:12.887 --> 00:01:13.770
- "'But I love you,

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.670
and I want to spend the
rest of my life with you.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:16.740
Will you marry me?'"

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.526
- She said, "Yes."

00:01:18.526 --> 00:01:21.137
And, we woke up the next morning,
she looked at me and said,

00:01:21.137 --> 00:01:22.295
"You still wanna do this?"

00:01:22.295 --> 00:01:23.128
I was like, "Yeah."

00:01:23.128 --> 00:01:25.180
- And my mom got sick, she
got diagnosed with cancer,

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:26.940
and so we knew that she
wasn't gonna make it.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.840
So we actually did a Justice
of the Peace ceremony

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:31.370
in December, but the wedding-wedding--

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:32.756
I just wanted a big party.

00:01:32.756 --> 00:01:33.740
- It was wonderful, it was awesome.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.360
- So after we got
married, he switched jobs.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.193
- Now we're working all the time,

00:01:37.193 --> 00:01:38.647
we don't really see much of each other.

00:01:38.647 --> 00:01:40.973
I'm getting up at 4:30 in
the morning and I'm out.

00:01:40.973 --> 00:01:43.910
- I think the things that
affected the marriage is,

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.840
just time away from each other between

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.060
his work and me doing theater.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:53.120
- I was just getting
more and more frustrated.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:53.953
Not with her.

00:01:53.953 --> 00:01:56.720
More with just, I really
don't like the way

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.430
my life is going at this point.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:00.470
The marriage was good.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:04.260
It was just, we got to a point we weren't

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:05.550
a married couple anymore,

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.840
we we're just two people
living in the same house,

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.410
and it needed to end.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.074
That was the end of the chapter.

00:02:11.074 --> 00:02:13.870
- He actually was the
one that brought it up.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.090
He was like, "I think we should separate."

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.730
- It was really tough, it was not easy.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.530
We basically went from
roommates who get along,

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.070
to roommates who don't get along,

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:24.320
who don't even want to be in
the same room with each other.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:25.420
- Obviously, it hurt.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:30.420
But looking back, it was the
right move for both of us.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.280
- I moved to New Orleans for six months.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.370
I was not in a good
place, drank way too much.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.270
She was one of the people I turned to.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.550
- I wanted to find a way
for us to be friends.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:43.610
I don't have a lot of people,
and I don't want to lose this.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.211
So I wanted to figure out
a way to remain friends.

00:02:46.211 --> 00:02:48.640
- Just kinda looking forward
to seeing these pictures

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.750
of people we haven't
seen in such a long time.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.500
- I think it might just kind of

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.769
give a little bit of closure.

00:02:56.769 --> 00:02:59.019
- I'm a little bit nervous.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.851
- [Austin] How are ya?

00:03:03.851 --> 00:03:07.980
- Yeah, super fun standing
outside of the door.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.150
- Waiting for people.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.998
- Yeah, I'm so patient.
- Yes you are.

00:03:10.998 --> 00:03:12.604
- You know how patient I am.

00:03:12.604 --> 00:03:13.459
I like this.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.292
- Thanks.

00:03:15.416 --> 00:03:16.716
I think, Buffalo Exchange?

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.163
Cool.

00:03:19.163 --> 00:03:19.996
- Cool.

00:03:19.996 --> 00:03:22.366
(laughing)

00:03:22.366 --> 00:03:24.410
So what lovely things
did you say about me?

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:25.853
- You're a terrible person.

00:03:25.853 --> 00:03:27.313
I was glad to be out of this.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:29.523
I don't know why I'm doing this--

00:03:29.523 --> 00:03:30.558
- Well, I'm super happy to be here.

00:03:30.558 --> 00:03:31.557
- I'm doing this for the money.

00:03:31.557 --> 00:03:32.580
- I'm gonna go.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.020
- Hopefully this isn't
one of those things that,

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:34.853
in concept--

00:03:34.853 --> 00:03:35.820
(laughing)

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.490
- It sounded like a good idea
but now after looking at it,

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:39.323
we're like--

00:03:39.323 --> 00:03:40.600
- No, I think it'll be fine.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:41.600
It'll be fine.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:42.786
Let's look at pictures.

00:03:42.786 --> 00:03:44.161
- You wanna look at these?

00:03:44.161 --> 00:03:45.624
- Should we do it?

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:46.457
- Alright.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:52.230
- I really seriously haven't
looked at these in forever.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:55.280
Aw look, there's your hair.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.870
- There's my hair, yeah.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.002
- What the fuck?

00:03:58.002 --> 00:04:00.252
(laughing)

00:04:03.412 --> 00:04:06.162
(soothing music)

00:04:13.403 --> 00:04:14.950
(laughing)

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:17.540
Honestly, there are a
lot of people here too,

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.480
that we don't--

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.310
- We don't see anymore or hear--

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:21.143
- Don't--

00:04:21.143 --> 00:04:21.976
Yeah.

00:04:21.976 --> 00:04:22.809
- - Or not hear anymore.

00:04:24.355 --> 00:04:26.700
You know, it's a good
reminder that things...

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:31.323
Things were good, and will be again.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.053
They are good.

00:04:38.139 --> 00:04:40.450
I think that there's a
stigma attached to divorce.

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:43.320
It's always gotta be bad,

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.380
and it doesn't always have to be bad.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.703
You kind of can choose
depending on the scenario.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.890
Just have as much respect for yourself,

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:55.220
and for the other person,
as humanly possible.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:58.273
Thank you for being here, and being you,

00:04:59.643 --> 00:05:01.113
and not just walking away.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:03.613
- Same.

00:05:03.613 --> 00:05:05.310
Thanks for sticking it out with me,

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.400
and wanting to still be my friend,

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.946
and making sure I was
okay when I got back.

00:05:11.946 --> 00:05:12.779
- Always.

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:13.800
- Cause I wasn't.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.210
- I know.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.360
- Could've easily gone
the other way, and--

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:21.540
- Okay, I'm gonna hug you.-

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:22.493
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.950
(soothing music)

